WEBVTT

00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:02.647
Checkpoint 1 focuses on recognition.

00:00:02.647 --> 00:00:07.162
Classify each variable as nominal, ordinal, interval, or ratio.

00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:12.067
For numeric variables, also decide whether the concept is counted or measured.

00:00:12.067 --> 00:00:15.692
Try to answer before opening the sample classifications.

00:00:15.692 --> 00:00:21.602
If you are unsure, return to the questions: label or quantity, ordered or unordered, true zero or not,

00:00:21.602 --> 00:00:26.467
counted or measured. For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:31.242
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:33.372
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:33.372 --> 00:00:39.982
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:39.982 --> 00:00:46.082
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:46.082 --> 00:00:51.717
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.829
not only whether the statement executes.
